|desc=The caster becomes an [[doom knight form|engine of destruction]], gaining a +1 [[attack bonus]] for every 2 caster levels, a +4 natural armor [[armor class|AC]] bonus, 20 [[strength]], 22 [[dexterity]], 18 [[constitution]], +5 to their [[fortitude]] [[saving throw]]s, and +1[[d6]] additional [[temporary hit point|hit point]]s per caster level.}}

==Notes==

* Although called a "natural armor bonus", the bonus is in fact a [[dodge bonus]], which [[stack]]s with other dodge bonuses toward the +20 cap.
* The temporary hit points are applied independently of the [[polymorph]], so these hit points can persist if the polymorph is canceled before the spell expires. (The reason for this is the reverse situation &mdash; losing the temporary hit points through damage will not cancel the polymorph.) This stacks over multiple castings.
* In addition to the stated benefits, this transformation grants the [[cleave]] feat, immunity to [[mind-affecting]] spells, and two additional [[free attack|free attacks]] [[attacks per round|per round]].
* A drawback to this spell is a possible lowering of [[armor class]] (since bonuses from items do not apply while transformed).
* While transformed by this spell, a character wields Tenser's Sword, a +3 [[longsword]] with a 1d6 [[fire damage]] bonus. (This may be detrimental to a character with [[monk]] levels.)
*Also while transformed, the caster's [[race]] becomes "[[elf]]", which might result in a [[multiclass penalty]]. It also allows a character to gain [[arcane archer]] levels at the expense of no longer being [[enforce legal character|legal]], if levels are taken while transformed.

